FWIW, the backend for what I wrote in the grant is not, at the moment, Stan-based.  It's just a slow R library.  But it could sure as hell stand to be Stanified, so that is my motivation to work on this.  If it benefits others, that's nice too, but really I just want to decouple some aspects of model fitting from model checking and model usage.  That's all I care about in my application.

I've never passed an array as anything other than column-major if I can help it.

I hadn't really considered encapsulating the data properly, since in my application, on the client side, it comes in one at a time, and on the server side, it's not supposed to be pulling the data in as JSON.  But column-major solves two problems at once, especially if you hint it:

"someData":
{
